WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.830
- All right, so let's end the hour

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:04.050
with something cool I've found
on the pages of social media.

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:05.096
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.096 --> 00:00:08.168
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.168 --> 00:00:10.665
So what started as a
passion for vintage clothes

00:00:10.665 --> 00:00:12.330
for two young men has turned into

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.490
a full-blown thriving business.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.830
And it's not just about
selling old school threads

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.990
but it's also about giving
the entire new school style

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.030
and inspiring others to do the same.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.490
It's good for business, it's
also good for the environment,

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.770
and TikTok is going crazy for the looks.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:27.101
Check this out.

00:00:27.101 --> 00:00:30.351
(upbeat playful music)

00:00:44.184 --> 00:00:46.333
(audience cheering)

00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:49.800
So cool and it's so throwback
nineties and I'm into it.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.900
We have these entrepreneurs on the line,

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.870
watching on Tampa Bay's MOR-TV
from Vintage Stock Reserve,

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.904
let's say hi to Tommy and Jordan.

00:00:56.904 --> 00:00:59.185
(audience cheering)

00:00:59.185 --> 00:01:00.018
- Hey Kelly.

00:01:00.018 --> 00:01:01.230
- Hey Kelly.
- What's up, y'all?

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:03.630
I'm so impressed by y'all, you're so cool.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.950
So Jordan, why don't you start.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:07.230
Explain more of how this got started.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.540
- So it all started when
my grandma introduced me

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:10.770
to the thrift shop.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:11.910
The first time I went in there,

00:01:11.910 --> 00:01:14.160
I was shocked with what
I was able to find,

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.800
and the unique items, it was just unreal.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.670
So when me and Tommy met, it
became a go-to hobby for us.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.740
Any chance we had, we
were in the thrift stores

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.030
to see what we could find.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:24.900
And before you know it,

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.570
we accumulated a collection
that was bigger than us.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:31.590
So we decided to share our
collection with the community

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.200
and start doing local pop-up markets.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.580
Every week, people were lined up

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.620
to see what we had to offer next.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:40.140
And we decided to teach ourselves to sew,

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.790
and that's when our upcycling journey

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.770
began to grow on TikTok.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.610
- That is so cool.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.920
So Tommy, you developed a
huge following on TikTok.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:50.190
So tell us about your upcycle challenges.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:51.810
- Yeah, so, when we first got on TikTok,

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.610
everyone was just doing these dance trends

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.740
and we wanted to switch it
up and do something new.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.440
So we started showing the
process of upcycling on TikTok

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.530
to promote a more sustainable
space in the fashion industry.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:04.500
One of our early videos
actually, is us reworking

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.930
a vintage Mickey Mouse bed
sheet into a bucket hat.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.780
And that video now has
over 28 million views.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.430
Another one of our popular videos

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.440
is us taking a green and gray sweater,

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.740
mixing and mashing it together
to create a fun, unique item.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:19.680
Now, Jordan and I do something
called the Upcycle Challenge

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.060
which is where we go to a thrift shop

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:23.310
with the budget of $10 and 10 minutes

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.650
to find things we normally wouldn't buy

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:27.420
and we spin a wheel to decide

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.100
what clothing item we're gonna make.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.960
And it's pretty much a
competition between us

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.880
to see who can make the cooler item,

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.130
and it's up to the audience
to vote in the comments

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.630
who does the best job.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.400
And through doing all of
this, we're able to educate

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.160
and inspire others to get
into sustainable fashion.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.320
- This is so rad you guys.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.450
I love it. Thank you so much, Tommy.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:46.500
Thank you, Jordan,

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.060
for the inspiration.
(audience cheering)

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.410
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.150
(heart dings)

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.590
And that's not all, fellas.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:55.200
Our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of FriXion,

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.210
the go-to erasable pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show",

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:00.150
want to celebrate those creating
fearlessly just like you.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.709
So they're gonna give you
$1,000. How's that sound?

00:03:02.709 --> 00:03:05.460
(audience cheering)

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:06.780
- Wow. Thank you so much.
- Thank you.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.485
- [Kelly] I love you guys.
- That means a lot.

00:03:08.485 --> 00:03:10.260
- [Kelly] I can't wait to see more videos.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.090
Keep inspiring us, all right?

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:12.923
- [Jordan] Thanks, Kelly.

00:03:12.923 --> 00:03:14.580
- Thank you having us.
- All right.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.380
Thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:19.290
Hillary Duff, Benjamin Levy Aguilar,

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.150
Reed, Pat, and Drake Milligan.

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:24.240
Y'all have a great day, and if
it's not, try and change it.

